theory SkyBridge_V2
begin

/* =================================================================
   SkyBridge Compass v2 -- Dolev-Yao symbolic model (Tamarin)

   This model REPLACES the earlier empty-adversary artifact
   (preserved as skybridge_v2_empty_adversary.spthy.bak). Every
   protocol message is sent with Out() and received with In(), so the
   built-in Dolev-Yao network adversary fully mediates the channel: it
   can drop, inject, reorder, replay, and synthesise messages from
   everything it has learned. Authentication, secrecy, agreement,
   forward secrecy and downgrade resistance are therefore proved
   against an *active* attacker -- not asserted by an unconditional
   action label as in the previous version.

   Protocol abstraction is derived from the authoritative sources:
     - rust/crates/skybridge-core/src/pqc_handshake.rs   (state machine,
       KEM encapsulate/decapsulate, transcript hashing, key derivation)
     - rust/crates/skybridge-core/src/classic_handshake.rs (classic path)
     - Sources/SkyBridgeProtocolCore/P2P/HandshakeMessages.swift
       (signaturePreimage of MessageA / MessageB; HMAC Finished)
     - Sources/SkyBridgeCore/P2P/TwoAttemptHandshakeManager.swift
       (fallback whitelist/blacklist, 300s/peer cooldown, downgrade gate)
     - Sources/SkyBridgeProtocolCore/P2P/CryptoSuite.swift
       (suite wire ids: classic 0x1001, PQCv1 0x0101, PQCv2/FS 0x0102)

   Suites modelled (negotiation state space is tiny and finite):
     SuiteClassic : X25519+Ed25519   (0x1001) -- classic, no PQC KEM
     SuitePQCv1   : ML-KEM-768        (0x0101) -- static KEM only
     SuitePQCv2   : ML-KEM-768-FS     (0x0102) -- static KEM + a fresh
                                                  ephemeral DH on BOTH
                                                  sides (FS suite)

   KEM abstraction (standard Tamarin KEM idiom):
     kempk(sk)         responder's static KEM public key
     kemenc(ss, pk)    ciphertext encapsulating fresh secret ss to pk
     kemdec(c, sk)     recovers ss iff c = kemenc(ss, kempk(sk))
   so KEM-derived secrecy is conditioned on holding the responder's
   long-term KEM secret -- exactly the v1 trust assumption.

   v2 forward secrecy: the v2 root absorbs an additional ephemeral DH
   secret 'g^(xa*xb)' that never travels in clear, so the key survives
   compromise of every long-term key as long as the ephemerals are not
   revealed.
   ================================================================= */

builtins: hashing, signing, diffie-hellman

functions:
    kempk/1,
    kemenc/2,
    kemdec/2

equations:
    kemdec(kemenc(ss, kempk(sk)), sk) = ss

/* Public suite tags. We use string constants 'Classic'/'PQCv1'/'PQCv2'
   directly in the rules, so no function declarations are needed. */

/* =================================================================
   Long-term identity (ML-DSA-65 signing key) + static KEM key
   ================================================================= */

/* Each device has exactly ONE long-term ML-DSA identity and ONE static
   KEM key (enforced by the once-restrictions below). This mirrors the
   real system where a device is provisioned with a single canonical
   identity that is what gets pinned -- it removes the spurious
   multi-identity confusion where an agent name could carry two keys. */
rule Register_Identity:
    [ Fr(~sk) ]
  --[ RegisterIdentity($A, pk(~sk)),
      OnlyOnceIdentity($A) ]->
    [ !Ltk($A, ~sk),
      !Pk($A, pk(~sk)),
      Out(pk(~sk)) ]

rule Register_KEMKey:
    [ Fr(~kemsk) ]
  --[ RegisterKEM($A, kempk(~kemsk)),
      OnlyOnceKEM($A) ]->
    [ !KemLtk($A, ~kemsk),
      !KemPk($A, kempk(~kemsk)),
      Out(kempk(~kemsk)) ]

restriction identity_once:
    "All A #i #j. OnlyOnceIdentity(A) @ #i & OnlyOnceIdentity(A) @ #j ==> #i = #j"

restriction kem_once:
    "All A #i #j. OnlyOnceKEM(A) @ #i & OnlyOnceKEM(A) @ #j ==> #i = #j"

/* =================================================================
   Out-of-band pairing pin (QR / TOFU pairing).
   Binds a peer identifier to BOTH the signing public key and the
   static KEM public key over an authentic OOB channel. The adversary
   cannot mint a pin; only the genuine published keys can be pinned.
   This is what makes identity binding / "identityMismatch" provable.
   ================================================================= */
rule Pair_OOB:
    [ !Pk($A, pkA),
      !KemPk($A, kpkA) ]
  --[ Pair($A, pkA, kpkA),
      OnlyOncePair($A) ]->
    [ !Pin($A, pkA, kpkA) ]

restriction pair_once:
    "All A #i #j. OnlyOncePair(A) @ #i & OnlyOncePair(A) @ #j ==> #i = #j"

/* =================================================================
   Key compromise (adversary capabilities)
   ================================================================= */

rule Reveal_Ltk:
    [ !Ltk($A, sk) ]
  --[ LtkReveal($A) ]->
    [ Out(sk) ]

rule Reveal_KEM:
    [ !KemLtk($A, kemsk) ]
  --[ KemReveal($A) ]->
    [ Out(kemsk) ]

/* Ephemeral reveal: the adversary may also corrupt a fresh ephemeral
   exponent (e.g. weak RNG / state compromise). Needed to state forward
   secrecy precisely (FS holds *unless* the ephemerals are revealed).  */
rule Reveal_Eph:
    [ !Eph(x) ]
  --[ EphReveal(x) ]->
    [ Out(x) ]

/* =================================================================
   Session-start / policy choice (3 policy modes), mirroring
   TwoAttemptHandshakeManager:
     'strictPQC'  : requirePQC, NO classic fallback   -> offers {v1,v2}
     'default'    : classic fallback allowed via local gate -> offers {v1,v2}
     'classicOnly': peer known classic-only            -> offers {Classic}
   Policy + offered set are bound into sigA's transcript.
   ================================================================= */

rule Init_Session_Strict:
    [ Fr(~sid), !Pin($B, pkB, kpkB) ]
  --[ Policy(~sid, 'strictPQC'),
      Offer(~sid, 'PQCv1'),
      Offer(~sid, 'PQCv2'),
      InitFor(~sid, $A, $B) ]->
    [ St_Init0(~sid, $A, $B, 'strictPQC', pkB, kpkB) ]

rule Init_Session_Default:
    [ Fr(~sid), !Pin($B, pkB, kpkB) ]
  --[ Policy(~sid, 'default'),
      Offer(~sid, 'PQCv1'),
      Offer(~sid, 'PQCv2'),
      InitFor(~sid, $A, $B) ]->
    [ St_Init0(~sid, $A, $B, 'default', pkB, kpkB) ]

rule Init_Session_ClassicOnly:
    [ Fr(~sid), !Pin($B, pkB, kpkB) ]
  --[ Policy(~sid, 'classicOnly'),
      Offer(~sid, 'Classic'),
      InitFor(~sid, $A, $B) ]->
    [ St_InitClassic0(~sid, $A, $B, 'classicOnly', pkB, kpkB) ]

/* =================================================================
   PQC v1 handshake (static KEM only) over the ACTIVE channel
   ================================================================= */

/* ---- I -> R : MessageA (PQCv1) ----
   Fresh KEM secret ~ss encapsulated to B's pinned static KEM key.
   transcript hash thA binds <sid,A,suite,cA,na,pkA> (the tuple Sha256'd
   in pqc_handshake.rs). sigA over DomA||thA-tuple with A's long-term key.
*/
rule I_SendA_PQCv1:
    [ St_Init0(sid, A, B, pol, pkB, kpkB),
      !Ltk(A, skA),
      Fr(~na),
      Fr(~ss) ]
  --[ OfferUsed(sid, 'PQCv1'),
      SendA(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1') ]->
    [ Out( <sid, '1', A, 'PQCv1', kemenc(~ss, kpkB), ~na,
            sign(<'DomA', sid, A, 'PQCv1', kemenc(~ss, kpkB), ~na, pk(skA)>, skA),
            pk(skA)> ),
      St_I_WaitB(sid, A, B, pol, 'PQCv1', pkB, kpkB, ~na, ~ss,
                 h(<sid, A, 'PQCv1', kemenc(~ss, kpkB), ~na, pk(skA)>)) ]

/* ---- R receives MessageA, decapsulates with pinned KEM secret, signs
   MessageB ----  responderShare empty for v1. sigB over
   DomB || thA || suite || share || nb || pkB. Session root = h(ss,...). */
rule R_RecvA_SendB_PQCv1:
    [ In( <sid, '1', A, 'PQCv1', cA, na, sigA, pkA> ),
      !Ltk(B, skB),
      !KemLtk(B, kemsk),
      !Pin(B, pk(skB), kempk(kemsk)),
      !Pin(A, pkA, kpkA),
      Fr(~nb) ]
  --[ Eq(verify(sigA, <'DomA', sid, A, 'PQCv1', cA, na, pkA>, pkA), true),
      VerifyA(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1'),
      RecvA(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1'),
      SelectedSuite(sid, 'PQCv1'),
      SigBIssued(sid, B, 'PQCv1'),
      Running_R(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1', h(<sid, A, 'PQCv1', cA, na, pkA>)),
      RootR(sid, h(<'root1', kemdec(cA, kemsk), na, ~nb>)) ]->
    [ Out( <sid, '2', B, 'PQCv1', 'noshare', ~nb,
            sign(<'DomB', h(<sid, A, 'PQCv1', cA, na, pkA>),
                  'PQCv1', 'noshare', ~nb, pk(skB)>, skB),
            pk(skB)> ),
      St_R_WaitFin(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1',
                   h(<'root1', kemdec(cA, kemsk), na, ~nb>),
                   h(<sid, A, 'PQCv1', cA, na, pkA>)) ]

/* ---- I receives MessageB, verifies sigB against pinned pkB, derives
   the same root, sends I->R Finished MAC. ---- */
rule I_RecvB_PQCv1:
    [ St_I_WaitB(sid, A, B, pol, 'PQCv1', pkB, kpkB, na, ss, thA),
      In( <sid, '2', B, 'PQCv1', 'noshare', nb,
           sigB, pkB> ) ]
  --[ VerifyB(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1'),
      Eq(verify(sigB, <'DomB', thA, 'PQCv1', 'noshare', nb, pkB>, pkB), true),
      RootI(sid, h(<'root1', ss, na, nb>)),
      Commit_I(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1', thA),
      Running_I_Fin(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1', thA) ]->
    [ Out( <sid, 'finI', h(<'macI', h(<'root1', ss, na, nb>), thA>)> ),
      St_I_WaitFin(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1', h(<'root1', ss, na, nb>), thA) ]

/* =================================================================
   PQC v2 handshake (static KEM + mandatory ephemerals = FS suite)
   ================================================================= */

/* ---- I -> R : MessageA (PQCv2) ----
   In addition to the KEM ciphertext, the initiator publishes a fresh
   ephemeral DH share 'g^~xa' (the v2 initiatorContribution). */
rule I_SendA_PQCv2:
    [ St_Init0(sid, A, B, pol, pkB, kpkB),
      !Ltk(A, skA),
      Fr(~na),
      Fr(~ss),
      Fr(~xa) ]
  --[ OfferUsed(sid, 'PQCv2'),
      SendA(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2'),
      EphI(sid, ~xa) ]->
    [ Out( <sid, '1', A, 'PQCv2', kemenc(~ss, kpkB), ~na, 'g'^~xa,
            sign(<'DomA', sid, A, 'PQCv2', kemenc(~ss, kpkB), ~na, 'g'^~xa, pk(skA)>, skA),
            pk(skA)> ),
      !Eph(~xa),
      St_I_WaitB_v2(sid, A, B, pol, 'PQCv2', pkB, kpkB, ~na, ~ss, ~xa,
                    h(<sid, A, 'PQCv2', kemenc(~ss, kpkB), ~na, 'g'^~xa, pk(skA)>)) ]

/* ---- R receives v2 MessageA, decapsulates, contributes its own fresh
   ephemeral 'g'^~xb (the mandatory v2 responderShare). The v2 root
   absorbs BOTH the KEM secret and the ephemeral DH secret g^(xa*xb). */
rule R_RecvA_SendB_PQCv2:
    [ In( <sid, '1', A, 'PQCv2', cA, na, gxa, sigA, pkA> ),
      !Ltk(B, skB),
      !KemLtk(B, kemsk),
      !Pin(B, pk(skB), kempk(kemsk)),
      !Pin(A, pkA, kpkA),
      Fr(~nb),
      Fr(~xb) ]
  --[ Eq(verify(sigA, <'DomA', sid, A, 'PQCv2', cA, na, gxa, pkA>, pkA), true),
      VerifyA(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2'),
      RecvA(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2'),
      SelectedSuite(sid, 'PQCv2'),
      SigBIssued(sid, B, 'PQCv2'),
      EphR(sid, ~xb),
      Running_R(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2', h(<sid, A, 'PQCv2', cA, na, gxa, pkA>)),
      RootR(sid, h(<'root2', kemdec(cA, kemsk), gxa^~xb, na, ~nb>)) ]->
    [ Out( <sid, '2', B, 'PQCv2', 'g'^~xb, ~nb,
            sign(<'DomB', h(<sid, A, 'PQCv2', cA, na, gxa, pkA>),
                  'PQCv2', 'g'^~xb, ~nb, pk(skB)>, skB),
            pk(skB)> ),
      !Eph(~xb),
      St_R_WaitFin(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2',
                   h(<'root2', kemdec(cA, kemsk), gxa^~xb, na, ~nb>),
                   h(<sid, A, 'PQCv2', cA, na, gxa, pkA>)) ]

/* ---- I receives v2 MessageB, verifies sigB, recomputes the hybrid
   root with the responder's ephemeral share. ---- */
rule I_RecvB_PQCv2:
    [ St_I_WaitB_v2(sid, A, B, pol, 'PQCv2', pkB, kpkB, na, ss, xa, thA),
      In( <sid, '2', B, 'PQCv2', gxb, nb, sigB, pkB> ) ]
  --[ VerifyB(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2'),
      Eq(verify(sigB, <'DomB', thA, 'PQCv2', gxb, nb, pkB>, pkB), true),
      RootI(sid, h(<'root2', ss, gxb^xa, na, nb>)),
      Commit_I(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2', thA),
      Running_I_Fin(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2', thA) ]->
    [ Out( <sid, 'finI', h(<'macI', h(<'root2', ss, gxb^xa, na, nb>), thA>)> ),
      St_I_WaitFin(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2', h(<'root2', ss, gxb^xa, na, nb>), thA) ]

/* =================================================================
   Classic handshake (X25519+Ed25519) -- only reachable via
   classicOnly policy or an explicitly-gated default fallback.
   Modelled with classic DH (no KEM). ===============================*/

/* default-policy local fallback gate: only a LOCAL capability error
   (pqcProviderUnavailable / suiteNegotiationFailed) plus a cooldown
   permit may move a default session into a classic attempt. Timeout /
   signature / replay / key-confirmation failures are NOT gateable. */
rule Default_LocalFallback_Gate:
    [ St_Init0(sid, A, B, 'default', pkB, kpkB) ]
  --[ FallbackGatePassed(sid, 'local_capability_error'),
      LocalFallbackEligible(sid),
      CooldownPermit(sid, 'allow'),
      Offer(sid, 'Classic'),
      DowngradeEvent(sid),
      DowngradeCtx(sid, 'local_capability_error', 'default') ]->
    [ St_Init_ClassicFallback(sid, A, B, 'default', pkB, kpkB) ]

/* I -> R MessageA classic (fresh DH share g^~ea). */
rule I_SendA_Classic:
    [ St_Init_ClassicFallback(sid, A, B, pol, pkB, kpkB),
      !Ltk(A, skA),
      Fr(~na),
      Fr(~ea) ]
  --[ OfferUsed(sid, 'Classic'),
      SendA(sid, A, B, 'Classic'),
      ClassicAttempt(sid),
      EphI(sid, ~ea) ]->
    [ Out( <sid, '1', A, 'Classic', 'g'^~ea, ~na,
            sign(<'DomA', sid, A, 'Classic', 'g'^~ea, ~na, pk(skA)>, skA),
            pk(skA)> ),
      !Eph(~ea),
      St_I_WaitB_C(sid, A, B, pol, 'Classic', pkB, ~na, ~ea,
                   h(<sid, A, 'Classic', 'g'^~ea, ~na, pk(skA)>)) ]

/* classicOnly policy emits MessageA classic directly. */
rule I_SendA_ClassicOnly:
    [ St_InitClassic0(sid, A, B, 'classicOnly', pkB, kpkB),
      !Ltk(A, skA),
      Fr(~na),
      Fr(~ea) ]
  --[ OfferUsed(sid, 'Classic'),
      SendA(sid, A, B, 'Classic'),
      ClassicAttempt(sid),
      EphI(sid, ~ea) ]->
    [ Out( <sid, '1', A, 'Classic', 'g'^~ea, ~na,
            sign(<'DomA', sid, A, 'Classic', 'g'^~ea, ~na, pk(skA)>, skA),
            pk(skA)> ),
      !Eph(~ea),
      St_I_WaitB_C(sid, A, B, 'classicOnly', 'Classic', pkB, ~na, ~ea,
                   h(<sid, A, 'Classic', 'g'^~ea, ~na, pk(skA)>)) ]

rule R_RecvA_SendB_Classic:
    [ In( <sid, '1', A, 'Classic', gea, na, sigA, pkA> ),
      !Ltk(B, skB),
      !KemLtk(B, kemsk),
      !Pin(B, pk(skB), kempk(kemsk)),
      !Pin(A, pkA, kpkA),
      Fr(~nb),
      Fr(~eb) ]
  --[ Eq(verify(sigA, <'DomA', sid, A, 'Classic', gea, na, pkA>, pkA), true),
      VerifyA(sid, A, B, 'Classic'),
      RecvA(sid, A, B, 'Classic'),
      SelectedSuite(sid, 'Classic'),
      SigBIssued(sid, B, 'Classic'),
      EphR(sid, ~eb),
      Running_R(sid, A, B, 'Classic', h(<sid, A, 'Classic', gea, na, pkA>)),
      RootR(sid, h(<'rootC', gea^~eb, na, ~nb>)) ]->
    [ Out( <sid, '2', B, 'Classic', 'g'^~eb, ~nb,
            sign(<'DomB', h(<sid, A, 'Classic', gea, na, pkA>),
                  'Classic', 'g'^~eb, ~nb, pk(skB)>, skB),
            pk(skB)> ),
      !Eph(~eb),
      St_R_WaitFin(sid, A, B, 'Classic',
                   h(<'rootC', gea^~eb, na, ~nb>),
                   h(<sid, A, 'Classic', gea, na, pkA>)) ]

rule I_RecvB_Classic:
    [ St_I_WaitB_C(sid, A, B, pol, 'Classic', pkB, na, ea, thA),
      In( <sid, '2', B, 'Classic', geb, nb, sigB, pkB> ) ]
  --[ VerifyB(sid, A, B, 'Classic'),
      Eq(verify(sigB, <'DomB', thA, 'Classic', geb, nb, pkB>, pkB), true),
      RootI(sid, h(<'rootC', geb^ea, na, nb>)),
      Commit_I(sid, A, B, 'Classic', thA),
      Running_I_Fin(sid, A, B, 'Classic', thA) ]->
    [ Out( <sid, 'finI', h(<'macI', h(<'rootC', geb^ea, na, nb>), thA>)> ),
      St_I_WaitFin(sid, A, B, 'Classic', h(<'rootC', geb^ea, na, nb>), thA) ]

/* =================================================================
   Finished / key confirmation (HMAC over transcript), both directions.
   Responder accepts only on a matching I->R Finished MAC; this is the
   point at which a session is considered Established for B. The
   initiator side establishes on a matching R->I Finished MAC.
   ================================================================= */

/* R sends its R->I Finished after MessageB; carried as a separate frame.
   (Modelled lazily: R emits it when it receives the initiator Finished,
   keeping the trace minimal but still requiring MAC agreement.) */
rule R_RecvFin_Establish:
    [ St_R_WaitFin(sid, A, B, suite, root, thA),
      In( <sid, 'finI', macI> ) ]
  --[ Eq(macI, h(<'macI', root, thA>)),
      KeyConfR(sid, A, B, suite),
      Commit_R(sid, A, B, suite, thA),
      SessionEstablished(sid, suite),
      SessionEstablishedFull(sid, A, B, suite),
      SecretRoot(sid, root) ]->
    [ Out( <sid, 'finR', h(<'macR', root, thA>)> ),
      St_R_Done(sid, A, B, suite, root) ]

rule I_RecvFin_Establish:
    [ St_I_WaitFin(sid, A, B, suite, root, thA),
      In( <sid, 'finR', macR> ) ]
  --[ Eq(macR, h(<'macR', root, thA>)),
      KeyConfI(sid, A, B, suite),
      Commit_I_Final(sid, A, B, suite, thA),
      SecretRoot(sid, root) ]->
    [ St_I_Done(sid, A, B, suite, root) ]

/* =================================================================
   Restriction: equality action label means literal equality.
   ================================================================= */
restriction Equality:
    "All x y #i. Eq(x, y) @ #i ==> x = y"

/* =================================================================
   ====================  LEMMAS  ===================================
   ================================================================= */

/* ---- Sanity / existence (anti-vacuity) ---- */

lemma Exists_PQCv1_Session:
    exists-trace
    "Ex sid A B #i.
        SessionEstablishedFull(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1') @ #i"

lemma Exists_PQCv2_Session:
    exists-trace
    "Ex sid A B #i.
        SessionEstablishedFull(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2') @ #i"

lemma Exists_Default_Classic_Downgrade:
    exists-trace
    "Ex sid A B #i #j.
        DowngradeEvent(sid) @ #i
      & SessionEstablishedFull(sid, A, B, 'Classic') @ #j"

/* ---- (5d-i) Negotiation integrity: the suite an initiator ACCEPTS
   (its sigB-verified Commit) must have been one it offered in that very
   session. This is exactly where the Rust initiator enforces
   offered_suites.contains(selected). (The responder's SelectedSuite over
   an attacker-forged MessageA is out of scope: with a compromised
   initiator key the attacker can mint any MessageA -- captured by the
   LtkReveal(A) escape on the agreement lemma below.) */
lemma NegotiationIntegrity_AcceptedWasOffered:
    all-traces
    "All sid A B sel thA #i.
        Commit_I(sid, A, B, sel, thA) @ #i
        ==> (Ex #j. Offer(sid, sel) @ #j)"

/* ---- Authentication core: a responder MessageB signature on a given
   transcript/suite can only exist if the pinned responder actually
   issued it (i.e. sigB is unforgeable under the pinned key), unless
   that responder's long-term signing key was revealed. This is the
   non-trivial replacement for the old unconditional VerifiedSigB. */
lemma SigB_Authentic_or_Compromised:
    all-traces
    "All sid A B suite thA #i.
        Commit_I(sid, A, B, suite, thA) @ #i
        ==> ( (Ex #j. SigBIssued(sid, B, suite) @ #j)
            | (Ex #r. LtkReveal(B) @ #r) )"

/* ---- (5b) Injective agreement initiator<->responder on
   <peerId, selectedSuite, transcript>. This is the security-critical
   direction: when the initiator A commits to a session with the pinned
   responder B on <A,B,suite,thA> (after verifying sigB), then B
   genuinely ran a responder session with matching data, AND the
   correspondence is injective -- no two distinct initiator commits map
   to the same responder run (replay/duplication of MessageB cannot make
   the initiator accept twice for one responder session). The agreement
   holds unless the responder's long-term signing key was revealed, in
   which case responder impersonation is unavoidable (expected escape). */
lemma Injective_Agreement_I_with_R:
    all-traces
    "All sid A B suite thA #i.
        Commit_I(sid, A, B, suite, thA) @ #i
        ==> ( ( (Ex #j. Running_R(sid, A, B, suite, thA) @ #j & #j < #i)
                & not (Ex sid2 #i2.
                         Commit_I(sid2, A, B, suite, thA) @ #i2
                       & not (#i2 = #i)) )
            | (Ex #r. LtkReveal(B) @ #r) )"

/* ---- (5a) Session-key secrecy: the established root secret of an
   honest session stays secret from the Dolev-Yao adversary, unless a
   relevant secret was revealed (see the precise per-suite FS lemmas
   below for which secret matters for which suite). Here we state the
   clean honest-case secrecy: with NO compromise of any long-term or
   ephemeral secret, the root is never known to the adversary. */
lemma Secrecy_SessionKey_HonestCase:
    all-traces
    "All sid root #i.
        SecretRoot(sid, root) @ #i
      & not (Ex A #r. LtkReveal(A) @ #r)
      & not (Ex A #r. KemReveal(A) @ #r)
      & not (Ex x #r. EphReveal(x) @ #r)
        ==> not (Ex #k. K(root) @ #k)"

/* ---- (5c-v1) Weak forward secrecy for v1: a v1 session root is
   secret as long as the responder's static KEM secret is not revealed
   (v1 has no ephemeral, so KEM-key compromise breaks it -- weak FS). */
lemma WeakFS_v1:
    all-traces
    "All sid A B root #i.
        SessionEstablishedFull(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1') @ #i
      & SecretRoot(sid, root) @ #i
      & not (Ex #r. KemReveal(B) @ #r)
      & not (Ex #r. LtkReveal(A) @ #r)
        ==> not (Ex #k. K(root) @ #k)"

/* ---- (5c-v1') The v1/v2 separation is REAL, not an artifact: there
   EXISTS a trace where a v1 session root is recovered by the adversary
   after the static KEM secret is revealed *later* (post-session) -- the
   exact post-compromise scenario v2 survives. This positive existence
   proof witnesses that v1 lacks forward secrecy, so WeakFS_v1's
   KEM-honest premise is load-bearing (not vacuous) and ForwardSecrecy_v2
   is a strictly stronger guarantee. */
lemma V1_LacksForwardSecrecy_Witness:
    exists-trace
    "Ex sid A B root #i #r #k.
        SessionEstablishedFull(sid, A, B, 'PQCv1') @ #i
      & SecretRoot(sid, root) @ #i
      & KemReveal(B) @ #r
      & K(root) @ #k
      & not (Ex x #e. EphReveal(x) @ #e)"

/* ---- (5c-v2) Genuine (perfect) forward secrecy for v2.

   This is the property v1 CANNOT achieve and the reason the FS suite
   (0x0102) exists. For a v2 session between an honest initiator and a
   matching honest responder run, the established root stays secret EVEN
   IF every long-term key -- the ML-DSA signing keys AND the static KEM
   key -- is subsequently revealed, provided the per-session ephemerals
   are not revealed.

   The standard PFS scoping applies: the long-term keys must be honest
   *at session time* (no LtkReveal of A or B strictly BEFORE the
   initiator commits at #i); reveals that happen LATER are exactly what
   forward secrecy must tolerate, and are allowed. (If B's signing key
   were already compromised before the session, the adversary is a live
   MITM on that very session -- a degenerate non-FS scenario that no
   key-agreement scheme can defend, witnessed in the earlier iteration
   by a forged MessageB carrying a degenerate ephemeral share.)

   Compare with WeakFS_v1 above: v1 needs the KEM key honest; v2 does
   not -- the ephemeral DH carries secrecy past full long-term
   compromise. */
lemma ForwardSecrecy_v2:
    all-traces
    "All sid A B root thA #i #j.
        RootI(sid, root) @ #i
      & Commit_I(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2', thA) @ #i
      & Running_R(sid, A, B, 'PQCv2', thA) @ #j
      & not (Ex x #r. EphReveal(x) @ #r)
      & not (Ex #r. LtkReveal(A) @ #r & #r < #i)
      & not (Ex #r. LtkReveal(B) @ #r & #r < #i)
        ==> not (Ex #k. K(root) @ #k)"

/* ---- (5e-i) Downgrade resistance under STRICT policy: an initiator
   running under strictPQC NEVER accepts a classic session. Because the
   only way to reach a classic initiator state is the default-policy
   fallback gate or the classicOnly policy, a strict session has no
   classic transition at all -- so neither a network/timeout effect nor
   an active attacker can drive the strict initiator to classic. Anchored
   on the initiator's sigB-verified Commit (policy is the initiator's). */
lemma NoClassicUnderStrictPQC:
    all-traces
    "All sid A B thA #i.
        Commit_I(sid, A, B, 'Classic', thA) @ #i
        ==> not (Ex #p. Policy(sid, 'strictPQC') @ #p)"

/* ---- (5e-ii) No silent classic fallback under default policy: whenever
   an initiator under default policy accepts a classic session, that
   acceptance is preceded by the explicit LOCAL fallback gate event
   (FallbackGatePassed with 'local_capability_error'). The adversary
   cannot manufacture this gate over the network; only the local
   capability path emits it. Hence timeout / dropped-PQC packets (which
   never emit the gate) cannot silently produce a classic session. */
lemma NoSilentClassicFallback_Default:
    all-traces
    "All sid A B thA #i.
        Commit_I(sid, A, B, 'Classic', thA) @ #i
      & (Ex #p. Policy(sid, 'default') @ #p)
        ==> (Ex #g. FallbackGatePassed(sid, 'local_capability_error') @ #g
                  & #g < #i)"

/* ---- Downgrade evidence: any classic session accepted by an initiator
   carries a context-bearing downgrade event (audit trail) OR was a
   classicOnly-policy session to begin with. There is no third way to a
   classic acceptance, so a classic session is always explained by
   recorded downgrade evidence or an explicit classic-only policy. */
lemma ClassicRequiresDowngradeOrClassicPolicy:
    all-traces
    "All sid A B thA #i.
        Commit_I(sid, A, B, 'Classic', thA) @ #i
        ==> ( (Ex #j. DowngradeEvent(sid) @ #j)
            | (Ex #p. Policy(sid, 'classicOnly') @ #p) )"

end
